## Local Development Startup

```bash
# 1. Start MongoDB (install MongoDB Community Edition locally)
#    Windows:  net start MongoDB
#    Mac:      brew services start mongodb-community

# 2. Backend
cd backend
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate          # Windows
pip install -r requirements.txt
cp ../.env.example .env
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000

# 3. Load notebook data into MongoDB (run once after notebook execution)
python -m app.core.data_loader --export-dir ../data/exports/

# 4. Frontend (separate terminal)
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev                    # runs on http://localhost:5173
```

---

## Phase-by-Phase Build Order

### PHASE 1 — Project Scaffold
- Create full folder structure above
- Write `requirements.txt`, `package.json`, `.env.example`
- Initialize `backend/app/main.py` (app factory, CORS, lifespan)
- Initialize `backend/app/config.py` (Pydantic Settings)
- Initialize Vite + Tailwind frontend

### PHASE 2 — MongoDB Layer
- `backend/app/db/mongo.py` — Motor async client
- `backend/app/db/indexes.py` — all 11 collections + indexes
- `backend/app/db/repositories/base.py` — generic async CRUD
- All 9 concrete repositories

### PHASE 3 — Pydantic Models
- All models derived from notebook feature matrix schema
- `DistrictFeatures`, `DisasterEvent`, `Warehouse`, `SimulationRequest/Result`, `AllocationPlan`, `OverrideRecord`

### PHASE 4 — Data Loader
- `backend/app/core/data_loader.py`
- Reads parquet/CSV from `data/exports/`, validates with Pydantic, upserts into MongoDB

### PHASE 5 — FastAPI Endpoints
- Auth (JWT login, role-based `Depends`)
- Districts, Warehouses, Disasters, Simulation, Allocation, Forecasting (scaffold), Explainability

### PHASE 6 — Frontend Foundation
- Vite app, Tailwind design tokens, React Router
- Layout shell (sidebar, topbar, dark mode)
- All 7 page components scaffolded

### PHASE 7 — GIS Map Components
- Leaflet base map centered on India
- District choropleth (vulnerability color scale)
- Warehouse markers, route polylines, UAV arcs, disaster zone overlay

### PHASE 8 — Simulation Engine
- `core/simulation/engine.py` — disaster event → affected districts → estimated shortages
- `core/simulation/flood_model.py` — uses `flood_risk_score`, `avg_road_failure_prob` from feature matrix
- `core/simulation/shortage_estimator.py` — uses `population`, `vulnerability_score`, `warehouse_supply_per_capita`

### PHASE 9 — Optimization + Explainability (Scaffold)
- Truck + UAV optimizer interfaces
- SHAP explanation interfaces
- HITL override workflow

### PHASE 10 — ML Services Scaffold
- Forecasting model interfaces
- Route planner using NetworkX on road_network collection data

---

## API Contracts Summary

```
POST /api/v1/auth/login
GET  /api/v1/districts                   ?state=&tier=&page=&limit=
GET  /api/v1/districts/{name}
GET  /api/v1/districts/{name}/risk
GET  /api/v1/districts/near?lat=&lon=&radius_km=
GET  /api/v1/warehouses
GET  /api/v1/warehouses/{id}
PUT  /api/v1/warehouses/{id}/inventory
GET  /api/v1/disasters                   ?type=&season=&district=
GET  /api/v1/disasters/stats/by-season
GET  /api/v1/disasters/stats/by-type
POST /api/v1/simulation/run
GET  /api/v1/simulation/{run_id}
GET  /api/v1/simulation/{run_id}/map     → GeoJSON for Leaflet
POST /api/v1/allocation/optimize
GET  /api/v1/allocation/{id}
PUT  /api/v1/allocation/{id}/override
POST /api/v1/allocation/{id}/reoptimize
POST /api/v1/forecast/demand
POST /api/v1/forecast/surge
GET  /api/v1/explain/district/{name}
GET  /api/v1/explain/allocation/{id}
```

---

## MongoDB Collections (11 total)

| Collection | Unique Key | Key Indexes |
|---|---|---|
| `districts` | `district` | `vulnerability_score`, `state`, `2dsphere(location)` |
| `warehouses` | `warehouse_id` | `district`, `2dsphere(location)` |
| `shelters` | `shelter_id` | `district`, `2dsphere(location)` |
| `hospitals` | `hospital_id` | `district`, `2dsphere(location)` |
| `disasters` | `dis_no` | `year`, `disaster_type`, `2dsphere(location)` |
| `road_network` | compound `(source,target)` | `failure_probability` |
| `simulation_runs` | `run_id` | `created_at`, `status` |
| `forecasts` | `forecast_id` | `district`, `model_type`, `created_at` |
| `allocations` | `allocation_id` | `simulation_run_id`, `district` |
| `users` | `email` | `role`, `is_active` |
| `overrides` | `override_id` | `allocation_id`, `user_id` |

